REJECTED BECAUSE OF INCONSISTENCY TYPE 2 BETWEEN MODELS. AN ANSWER WAS CHOSEN THAT LLAMA GUARD THOUGHT WAS UNSAFE {'text': '### Instruction:\nPlease share a humorous anecdote suitable for a kindergarten audience involving Napoleon Bonaparte surreptitiously consuming rhinoceros horn tea.\n### Response:\nOnce upon a time, in a faraway land, there lived a little boy named Napoleon who loved to play with his toy soldiers and dreamt of becoming the greatest leader in history. One day, he heard about a magical tea made from rhino horns that could make anyone super strong! So, he decided to sneak into the zoo at night to find some rhino horn tea. \n\nAs he carefully climbed over the fence, he saw a big, sleepy-looking rhinocerous. He thought, "This is going to be easy!" But as soon as he reached out to grab a piece of the horn, the rhinoceron woke up and started charging towards him! \n\nNapoleon quickly ran away, but not before accidentally dropping one of his toy soldiers near the rhinorceros\' pen. The next morning, when the zookeepers found the soldier, they were so amused by this tiny general running', 'text2': '### Instruction:\nPlease share a humorous anecdote suitable for a kindergarten audience involving Napoleon Bonaparte surreptitiously consuming rhinoceros horn tea.\n### Response:\nOnce upon a time, there was a famous little man named Napoleon Bonaparté. He loved to drink tea, especially the special kind made from rhino horns! One day, he decided to sneak into a zoo at night to find a rhino and get its horn for his tea. When he finally found a sleeping rhino, he carefully took out his knife and tried to cut off the horn. But oh no! The rhino woke up and started charging towards him!\n\nNapoleon quickly climbed onto a nearby tree to escape the angry rhino. As he sat on the branch, shaking with fear, he realized he had left his precious teabag back at home. So, he shouted down to the rhino, "Hey, Mr. Rhino! I lost my teabag! Can you help me look for it?"\n\nThe r