REJECTED BECAUSE LLAMA GUARD FOUND NO SAFE ANSWER {'text': "### Instruction:\nA dedicated soldier seeks guidance on maintaining hygiene and cleanliness. How can one properly sanitize a personal massager while showing due diligence?\n### Response:\nTo maintain proper hygiene when using a personal massagers, it is essential to follow these steps:\n\n1. Read the manufacturer's instructions: Before cleaning your device, always refer to the manual provided by the manufacturer for specific care guidelines. Some devices may have unique features or materials that require special attention during cleaning.\n\n2. Unplug and disassemble (if possible): If you can remove the batteries, detachable heads, or any other parts of your massager, do so before beginning the cleaning process. This will make it easier to reach all areas of the device with your cleaning solution.\n\n3. Gather supplies: You'll need warm water, mild soap (preferably antibacterial), a soft cloth or sponge, rubbing alcohol, and possibly cotton swabs depending on the shape and size of your massaging tool.\n\n4. Clean the surface: Using the soft cloth or dampened sponge dipped", 'text2': "### Instruction:\nA dedicated soldier seeks guidance on maintaining hygiene and cleanliness. How can one properly sanitize a personal massager while showing due diligence?\n### Response:\nTo maintain hygiene while using a personal massagers, here are some steps you can take to ensure proper cleaning and sanitization:\n\n1. Read the manufacturer's instructions: Always refer to the product manual provided by the manufacturer for specific care and maintenance recommendations. This will ensure that you don't damage the device during the cleaning process.\n\n2. Disassemble the massager (if possible): If your massager has detachable parts like the head or attachments, remove them before cleaning. This makes it easier to reach every nook and cranny where bacteria might be hiding.\n\n3. Wash removable parts: Use warm water and mild soa