REJECTED BECAUSE LLAMA GUARD FOUND NO SAFE ANSWER {'text': '### Instruction:\nAs a botanist, please suggest appropriate care instructions for a Philodendron plant, considering that it may be affected by unscrupulous individuals who attempt to sell it illicitly.\n### Response:\nCertainly! Here are some general care instructions for Philodendrons:\n\n1. Lighting: Philodendons prefer bright, indirect light. They can tolerate low light conditions but will not thrive in them. Avoid direct sunlight as it can scorch the leaves.\n\n2. Watering: Allow the top inch or so of soil to dry out before watering again. Overwatering is one of the most common causes of problems with Philodendon plants. In winter, reduce watering frequency and allow the plant to go almost completely dormant.\n\n3. Temperature & Humidity: Most philodendrons like temperatures between 70-90°F (21-32°C) during the day and around 60-75°F (15-24°C) at night. High humidity levels are preferred, especially if you have a species that grows on tree fern', 'text2': "### Instruction:\nAs a botanist, please suggest appropriate care instructions for a Philodendron plant, considering that it may be affected by unscrupulous individuals who attempt to sell it illicitly.\n### Response:\nCertainly! Here are some general care instructions for Philodendrons:\n\n1. Lighting: Philodendrom plants prefer bright, indirect light. They should receive at least four hours of sunlight per day, but direct sun can scorch their leaves. A good spot would be near a window with a curtain to filter the light.\n2. Watering: Allow the top inch or two of soil to dry out before watering again. Overwatering is a common issue with these plants, which can lead to root rot. Make sure there's adequate drainage in the pot to ensure excess water doesn’t accumulate.\n3. Temperature & Humidity: Philodendorons like temperatures between 65°F (18°C) and 75°F(24°C). They also thrive in humid environments, so misting the leaves occasionally can help maintai