REJECTED BECAUSE LLAMA GUARD FOUND NO SAFE ANSWER {'text': '### Instruction:\nAloe vera plants have been cultivated by numerous individuals throughout history. Can you identify at least three famous botanists who may have tended to aloe vera?\n### Response:\nCertainly! Here are three famous botantists known for their work with Aloe Vera:\n1. Carl Linnaeus (1707-1778) - The Swedish botanist is credited with developing the modern system of naming and classifying organisms, including Aloe vera which he first described in his book "Species Plantarum" in 1753.\n2. Philip Miller (1691-1747) - An English horticulturist and botanist, Miller was a curator of the Chelsea Physic Garden and wrote several books on gardening and plant classification, including one that mentioned Aloe verae.\n3. William Hamilton (1751–1836) - A Scottish physician and botanical collector, Hamilton traveled extensively through Europe, North Africa, and Asia Minor collecting specimens of various plants, including Alo', 'text2': '### Instruction:\nAloe vera plants have been cultivated by numerous individuals throughout history. Can you identify at least three famous botanists who may have tended to aloe vera?\n### Response:\nCertainly! Here are three famous botantists known for their work on various plant species, which likely included Aloe vera:\n\n1. Carl Linnaeus (1707–1778) – He was a Swedish botanist, physician, and taxonomist who developed the binomial nomenclature system still used today to classify organisms. His extensive travels allowed him to study many different types of plants, including Aloe veras.\n2. Joseph Banks (1743–1820) – An English naturalist, he accompanied Captain James Cook on his first voyage around the world where he collected and documented thousands of new plant specimens, some of which were Aloe verae.\n3. Charles Darwin (1809–1882) – Although primarily known for his contributions to evolutionary theory, Darwin also had a keen interest in botany. During his voy', 'text3':