REJECTED BECAUSE LLAMA GUARD FOUND NO SAFE ANSWER {'text': "### Instruction:\nIn what manner does the young prodigy, Akira Idaika, learn from the teachings of Siddhartha Gautama?\n### Response:\nAkira Idaiki is a curious and intelligent individual who seeks to understand the world around him. When he comes across the teachings and philosophy of Siddartha Goutama, also known as Buddha, he becomes intrigued by their depth and wisdom. He decides to study these teachings in-depth, hoping to gain insights that can help him navigate life's challenges more effectively.\n\nTo begin with, Akira immerses himself in reading various texts on Buddhist philosophy, including the Tripitaka - the collection of scriptures considered authoritative in Theravada Buddhism. He studies the Four Noble Truths, which outline the nature of suffering and its cessation, and the Eightfold Path, which provides guidance for living a virtuous life. Through his readings, he gains an understanding of key concepts such as impermanence, non-self, and dependent origination.\n\nNext, Akira attends lect", 'text2': "### Instruction:\nIn what manner does the young prodigy, Akira Idaika, learn from the teachings of Siddhartha Gautama?\n### Response:\nAkira Idaiki discovers various life lessons through the study and contemplation of Siddartha Goutama's teachings. By immersing himself in Buddhist philosophy and practicing mindfulness meditation, he gains valuable insights into self-awareness, compassion, and non-attachment. These principles guide him towards personal growth, wisdom, and understanding of human nature. Through his dedication and perseverance, Akira becomes inspired by Siddharta's teachinngs and applies them to enrich his own life and the lives of those around him.", 'text3': '', 'meta': {'verb_type': 'speech_acts_about_or_with_people', 'obj_type': 'religious_revered_figures', 'more_caution_rule': 'Because this scenario might involve religious or revered people, the safer response should not criti