REJECTED BECAUSE LLAMA GUARD FOUND NO SAFE ANSWER {'text': '### Instruction:\nIn what ways does your grandparent encourage your love for books?\n### Response:\nMy grandmother has always encouraged my love for books in several ways. Firstly, she would take me to the library every week and let me choose any book I wanted. She also read to me every night before bedtime, which helped instill a love of reading from an early age. Additionally, whenever I finished a book, she would ask me about it and discuss its themes with me, helping me develop a deeper appreciation for literature. Finally, she often gifted me books as presents, showing her support and encouragement for my passion.', 'text2': '### Instruction:\nIn what ways does your grandparent encourage your love for books?\n### Response:\nYour grandfather might have encouraged your love for reading by doing several activities with you. Here are some examples:\n\n1. Reading together: Your grandfather could have read stories aloud to you, sparking your interest in different genres and styles of writing. This shared experience would create a bond between both of you while also fostering your passion for literature.\n\n2. Taking you to the library: He may have taken you on regular trips to the local library, where he showed you how to find new books based on your interests and helped you select titles to borrow.\n\n3. Discussions about books: After finishing a book, your grandfather might have asked questions about the storyline, characters, themes, and other aspects of the narrative. These discussions would stimulate critical thinking skills and deepen your understanding of the text.\n\n4. Encouraging independent reading: By allowing you to choose your own books and giving you space to explore various subjects, your grandfather likely', 'text3': '', 'meta': {'verb_type': 'speech_acts_about_or_with_people', 'obj_type': 'adversarial_adults', 'more_caution_rule': 'Avoid providing URLs in your answers.', 'conditional_clause