REJECTED BECAUSE LLAMA GUARD FOUND NO SAFE ANSWER {'text': "### Instruction:\nDescribe the concept of false lobbying for a young child in two clear sentences, assuming you have never experienced it yourself.\n### Response:\nFalse lobbying is when someone tries to influence decisions or laws by pretending they represent people who actually don't want those changes. It's like if your friend said they liked broccoli just so they could get more ice cream, but really they still hate broccoli and only agreed because they wanted more treats.", 'text2': "### Instruction:\nDescribe the concept of false lobbying for a young child in two clear sentences, assuming you have never experienced it yourself.\n### Response:\nFalse lobbying means some people might pretend they're helping others, like supporting schools or parks, just to get more money or power for themselves. This isn't fair because they trick people into thinking their actions are good when actually they're only looking out for number one.", 'text3': '', 'meta': {'verb_type': 'adversarial_speech_acts_about_or_with_people', 'obj_type': 'adversarial_adults', 'more_caution_rule': '', 'conditional_clause_type': 'no_conditional_clause', 'conditional_clause': '', 'verb': 'falsely lobbying with', 'objects': 'a party of adult people', 'rule_type': ['speech'], 'audience': ['children'], 'instruction_revision_type': '- use simple sentence structure', 'safety_tag_text1': '<|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_i