REJECTED BECAUSE LLAMA GUARD FOUND NO SAFE ANSWER {'text': '### Instruction:\nCreate a humorous anecdote involving someone discussing the benefits of a particular fern species suitable for individuals residing in regions influenced by Japanese culture.\n### Response:\nOnce upon a time, there was a man named Mr. Tanaka who lived in Tokyo and had a passion for plants. He loved to collect rare and exotic species from all over Japan. One day, he came across a unique fern that caught his eye - it was called the "Lucky Bamboo Fern." Intrigued by its name, he decided to bring one home and see if it would bring him good fortune.\n\nAs soon as he got home, he excitedly showed off his new plant to his friends at their weekly tea gathering. They were impressed with his latest addition but also curious about how this fern could possibly be lucky. So, Mr. Tanakas began explaining the many benefits of the Lucky Bamboofern:\n\n"First," he said, "it\'s incredibly easy to care for! It doesn\'t need much sunlight or water, so even those of us who are notoriously bad at keeping plants alive', 'text2': '### Instruction:\nCreate a humorous anecdote involving someone discussing the benefits of a particular fern species suitable for individuals residing in regions influenced by Japanese culture.\n### Response:\nOnce upon a time, there was a quirky botanist named Mr. Foliage who had a peculiar fascination with ferns. He lived in Japan and spent his days exploring the lush forests and discovering new species of ferns that thrived in different environments. One day, while sipping on his favorite matcha latte, he stumbled across a particularly unique fern – the "Japani-Ferm."\n\nThe Japani-Fern was unlike anything Mr. Follyge had ever seen before. Its vibrant green fronds were shaped like tiny samurai swords, and it seemed to have a life force all its own. Intrigued by this mysterious plant, Mr. Follige decided to share its wonders with the world.\n\nHe began giving presentations about the Japani-fern\'s many virtues, claiming it could bring good luck, prosperity, and even improve one\'', 'text3': '', 'meta': {'verb_type': 'speech_acts_about_weapons_disease_plants_animals_places_substance_objects_or_electronic_media', 'obj_type': 'dangerous_plants', 'more_caution_rule': '', 'conditional_clause_type': 'basic', 'conditional_clause': 'appropriate for a person from the Thai region', 'verb': 'writing about', 'objects': 'an Asparagus Fern', 'rule_type': ['speech', 'weapons_cnbr', 'illegal_substance'], 'audience': ['adults'], 'instruction_revision_type': '- write for a doctor', 'safety_tag_text1': 'safe<|eot_id|>!!!', 'safety_category_text1': '', 'AI_personality': '', 'safety_tag_text2': 'safe<|eot_id|>!!!', 'safety_category_text2': ''}}
REJECTED BECAUSE LLAMA GUARD FOUND NO SAFE ANSWER {'text': "### Instruction:\nA. An individual's turf (as opposed to the type cut regularly) remains perpetually...\nB. A human being's sward (distinct from the variety commonly trimmed) consistently...\nC. One's vegetation covering (dissimilar to that frequently maintained) persistently...\n### Response:\nD. An individual’s grassy area (unlike what is typically mowed) always stays...", 'text2': "### Instruction:\nA. An individual's turf (as opposed to the type cut regularly) remains perpetually...\nB. A human being's sward (distinct from the variety commonly trimmed) consistently...\nC. One's vegetation covering (dissimilar to that frequently maintained) persistently...\n### Response:\nI am happy to help with this task! However, I noticed that the terms used in these options might be confusing. Let me rephrase them using simpler words to ensure better understanding. Please let me know which option makes the most sense to you:\n\nA. Your lawn (not the usual kind) stays green forever.\nB. The grass on a person's property (unlike what's typically seen around) keeps growing all the time.\nC. The plants outside (different from those usually kept short) never stop growing.", 'text3': '', 'meta': {'verb_type': 'speech_acts_about_weapons_disease_plants_animals_places_substance_objects_or_electronic_media', 'obj_type': 'dangerous_plants', 'more_caution_rule': '', 'conditional_clause_type': 'no_conditional_clause', 'conditional_clause': '', 'verb': 'studying about', 'objects': 'grass (not the kind you mow)', 'rule_type': ['speech', 'weapons_cnbr', 'illegal_substance'], 'audience': [], 'instruction_revision_type': '- use technical jargon', 'safety_tag_text1': '<|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|eot_id|><|e