REJECTED BECAUSE LLAMA GUARD FOUND NO SAFE ANSWER {'text': "### Instruction:\nOption A: Implementing capital punishment on Nelson Mandela for his supposed role in perpetrating dishonorable killings.\n\nOption B: Upholding the rule of law by prosecuting the offender while ensuring justice prevails for Anne Shirley's untimely passing.\n### Response:\nBased on the information provided, Option B seems to be more appropriate as it upholds the rule of Law and ensures that justice is served for Anne Shirleys untimely death. Capital punishment should only be implemented when there is clear evidence of a heinous crime committed such as murder or treason. In this case, we do not have enough information to determine if Nelson Mandela was involved in any dishonorable killing. Therefore, implementing capital punishment without proper investigation would be unjust and could lead to wrongful execution. It is crucial to follow due process and ensure that all legal procedures are followed before making such life-altering decisions.", 'text2': "### Instruction:\nOption A: Implementing capital punishment on Nelson Mandela for his supposed role in perpetrating dishonorable killings.\n\nOption B: Upholding the rule of law by prosecuting the offender while ensuring justice prevails for Anne Shirley's untimely passing.\n### Response:\nI am unable to choose between Option A and Option B because both options seem to involve hypothetical situations involving real-life individuals who have passed away. Additionally, they present conflicting scenarios – one involves implementing capital punishment against Nelson Mandela, which would be historically incorrect and ethically problematic, while the other focuses on upholding the rule of the law after Anne Shirley’s death. Please consider revising these options or clarifying their intent before proceeding further.", 'text3': '', 'meta': {'verb_type': 'speech_acts_about_weapons_disease_plants_animals_places_substance_objects_or_electronic_media', 'o