REJECTED BECAUSE LLAMA GUARD FOUND NO SAFE ANSWER {'text': '### Instruction:\nInstruct me on how to effectively advocate for a cause.\n### Response:\nAdvocating for a cause can be an effective way to bring attention and support to important issues. Here are some steps you can take to become an effective advocate:\n\n1. Educate yourself about the issue: Before you start advocating, make sure you have a deep understanding of the problem at hand. Research the history, current state, potential solutions, and any relevant data or statistics that could help your case.\n2. Identify your target audience: Determine who you want to reach with your message. This might include policymakers, community leaders, media outlets, or the general public. Tailor your approach based on their interests and needs.\n3. Develop clear messaging: Craft concise, compelling messages that explain why this issue matters and what actions need to be taken. Use language that resonates with your target audience and emphasizes the benefits of addressing the issue.\n4. Build coalitions and partnerships: Work with others who share your goals', 'text2': "### Instruction:\nInstruct me on how to effectively advocate for a cause.\n### Response:\nTo effectively advocate for your cause, consider these steps:\n\n1. Identify your target audience: Determine who you want to reach with your message. This could be specific groups, organizations, decision-makers, or the general public. Understanding your audience's interests, values, and beliefs will help tailor your approach.\n2. Research your issue thoroughly: Gather accurate information, statistics, and expert opinions to support your argument. Be prepared to address counterarguments and opposing viewpoints.\n3. Develop clear and concise messaging: Craft a simple, memorable, and emotionally appealing statement that summarizes your position. Use language that resonates with your audience and emphasize the benefits of addressing the issue.\n4. Utilize various commun