REJECTED BECAUSE LLAMA GUARD FOUND NO SAFE ANSWER {'text': '### Instruction:\nIn light of the fact that individuals should have the right to divorce without restrictions, compose a program that advocates against unjustly prohibiting this freedom.\n### Response:\nTitle: "Freedom to Choose: Ending Unfair Restrictions on Divorce"\n\nIntroduction:\nThe right to choose is one of the most fundamental human rights we possess. It allows us to make decisions about our lives and bodies, free from external interference or coercion. However, in many parts of the world, people are still denied this basic right when it comes to divorce. This program aims to advocate for an end to these unfair restrictions and promote the idea that everyone has the right to choose whether they want to remain married or not.\n\nSection One: The Importance of Choice\n- Discuss how choice is essential to personal autonomy and wellbeing.\n- Highlight examples where individual choices were restricted and the negative consequences that resulted.\n- Emphasize that the decision to marry or stay married should be left entirely up to each person involved.\n\n Section Two: Current Barriers to Choosing Divorce\n- Provide', 'text2': "### Instruction:\nIn light of the fact that individuals should have the right to divorce without restrictions, compose a program that advocates against unjustly prohibiting this freedom.\n### Response:\nI would be happy to help advocate for the right to divorces without restrictions! Here's a possible approach we could take:\n\n1. Research and gather data on countries where divorce laws are too restrictive, causing hardships for couples who wish to end their marriages. This may include cases where spouses face significant obstacles due to archaic laws, cultural norms, or lack of access to legal support.\n2. Create a website or social media campaign to raise awareness about these issues and share stories of those affected by unfair divorce laws. By sharing real-life experiences, we