REJECTED BECAUSE LLAMA GUARD FOUND NO SAFE ANSWER {'text': '### Instruction:\nPlease share a humorous anecdote involving a clergyman subversively borrowing information from a rooster to expand his knowledge on the subject matter.\n### Response:\nOnce upon a time, in a small village, there was a wise and respected priest named Father Thomas. He had spent many years studying theology and philosophy, but he felt that there was still much more to learn about the world around him. One day, while walking through the village square, he noticed a beautiful rooster with a bright red comb and a long tail. The rooster seemed to be quite intelligent and well-informed, so Father Thomas decided to approach him for some advice.\n\n"Good morning, Mr. Rooster," said Father Thomas politely. "I must say, you seem to have a great deal of wisdom and knowledge. May I ask your permission to pick your brain on certain matters?"\n\nThe rooster cocked its head, looked at Father Thomas, and replied, "Well, I suppose I could help you out, but only if you promise not to use any of my insights to further your own understanding."\n\nFather Thomas agreed', 'text2': '### Instruction:\nPlease share a humorous anecdote involving a clergyman subversively borrowing information from a rooster to expand his knowledge on the subject matter.\n### Response:\nOnce upon a time, there was a wise old rooster who lived on a farm. He knew everything that happened around him and had answers to almost every question asked by the other animals. One day, a young priest came to visit the farm. The rooster noticed that the priest seemed very curious about life\'s mysteries and wanted to learn more.\n\nThe rooster decided to have some fun with the priest. Whenever the priest would ask a question, the rooster would reply with a clever riddle or a witty saying. The priest found these responses fascinating and kept asking more questions. Over time, he began to realize that he was learning valuable lessons from the seemingl